SUMMARY:
Enterprise resource planning (ERP) has become key to businesses everywhere, a=
nd many corporate ERP implementations depend on SAP software. IT professional=
s must build bulletproof infrastructures that enterprises can rely on for the=
ir SAP ERP applications.
          =20
Listen to this podcast as Anastasia Hurley of HP and Stan Gibson of TechTarge=
t discuss how SQL Server consolidation can deliver a highly available, inhere=
ntly scalable and easy-to-manage infrastructure for ERP systems.

This is the second in a three-part podcast series on the topic of SQL Server =
consolidation. The first podcast examines the problem of server sprawl and ho=
w IT can get it under control, and the third will explain how a range of Wind=
ows applications can be optimized within an adaptive infrastructure.














